<body>
    <h1>Meeting Minutes of 2026/07/27 - Q2 reporting</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p local-id=3D"9af512e1472b">Hi all,</p>
<p local-id=3D"4af405f9f914">Thank you for your attendance. Please find the=
 meeting minutes below.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6e60bbfbfb5f">Date: Monday, 27th July, 2026<br>
Time: [Please add] HK Time<br>
Attendees: [Please confirm attendees]</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"92b7757352ec" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/27-Q2reporting-=
QuickRecap">Quick Recap</h2>
<p local-id=3D"aee0a52c2984">This meeting focused on AI knowledge sharing a=
nd progress updates across the project layers. Daijiang Xie introduced STOA=
G (Self-Training On-Going Agent), an enhanced RAG-agent approach that uses =
a controller to determine whether the available evidence is sufficient and =
to identify information gaps for targeted follow-up retrieval. The Data Pro=
cessing Layer completed semantic segmentation and card-system development. =
The Tool Layer tested an English financial QA dataset and explored re-ranki=
ng and BM25 tokenization improvements, while identifying issues with recall=
 quality and chunking. The Integration Layer presented CPR-system enhanceme=
nts, including multi-turn tool calling, short-term memory, and query rewrit=
ing. The Monitoring Layer developed frontend observability features. The me=
eting also confirmed that a document-listing function can be implemented se=
curely through appropriate permission controls.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"ebb83a64de0c" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/27-Q2reporting-=
Follow-upActions">Follow-up Actions</h2>
<p local-id=3D"a1bc4d00e2cb">Huifang Liu</p>
<ul local-id=3D"086070c1-1b3d-4662-9810-f5c9fa9e8b5f">
<li local-id=3D"a44b3b82-52a0-4475-894a-dd616d37ed6b">
<p local-id=3D"ee4b1781b224">Integrate the completed query-understanding co=
mponents into the main workflow.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6f851d4a-6ab9-4afd-868a-d04358eaf482">
<p local-id=3D"9f0a8d798e3a">Upload relevant local unit tests to Confluence=
.</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"0dc99e5c58fc">Jiaxing Dai</p>
<ul local-id=3D"3df06335-449c-4209-a1a7-29f614e68a30">
<li local-id=3D"6048dba9-0d29-43d4-9d86-7f3111451464">
<p local-id=3D"fdfb021013e5">Experiment with alternative embedding models, =
including different dimensions or model types, to improve retrieval quality=
.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"808a1658-ff31-4cb9-add6-cdb0babdbd33">
<p local-id=3D"434746a900fe">Evaluate and, if appropriate, adjust the chunk=
 aggregation strategy, such as ranking multiple chunks together.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c636cfe2-dbb3-40a2-9b69-d657b503fb4b">
<p local-id=3D"231c48e5ea50">Evaluate and, if appropriate, revise the chunk=
ing strategy from fixed-length splitting to paragraph-based splitting.</p><=
/li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"6e0de392dca5">Daijiang Xie</p>
<ul local-id=3D"a57ba27d-0a86-4b54-b2e9-6011c7b201a9">
<li local-id=3D"b189a3d0-24fb-4058-89d6-5daaba9ac39f">
<p local-id=3D"58ec6cdf1428">Share the STOAG paper link in the meeting grou=
p.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"3f8b5fc72d3a" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/27-Q2reporting-=
Collaboration">Collaboration</h2>
<p local-id=3D"e5b1249902c8">All members:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"92a13142-2070-445f-a36d-1e15d6c3a6f9">
<li local-id=3D"d5b7a15e-69cb-4bec-ac02-6ce2c93b0ff8">
<p local-id=3D"ddbc769cf971">Upload this week=E2=80=99s completed technical=
 documentation to the designated Confluence folder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"93635ee2-4b49-42b9-810f-24c18c65fda6">
<p local-id=3D"04cb46ad7669">Continue improving layer-specific functionalit=
y and prepare for integration testing next week.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"15a06dc7810f" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/27-Q2reporting-=
Summary">Summary</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"465acc45626b" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/27-Q2reporting-=
STOAGKnowledgeSharing">STOAG Knowledge Sharing</h3>
<p local-id=3D"ea0dcbd46c60">Daijiang Xie shared STOAG, a solution designed=
 to improve Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) agents in multi-hop questi=
on-answering scenarios. Traditional RAG agents may stop retrieval too early=
 or continue searching unnecessarily. STOAG addresses this issue by introdu=
cing a controller that evaluates whether the current evidence is sufficient=
 to answer the question.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4135a4eac62e">The controller examines evidence sufficiency a=
nd identifies missing information. If the available evidence is adequate, r=
etrieval stops. Otherwise, the system generates structured information-gap =
descriptions to guide the next retrieval round. Daijiang suggested integrat=
ing this approach into the current project, potentially through the evidenc=
e-context component.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"fb03b22aa7b7" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/27-Q2reporting-=
IterativeRetrievalDiscussion">Iterative Retrieval Discussion</h3>
<p local-id=3D"2cf43da11290">Tao asked for an example of iterative retrieva=
l. Daijiang explained that the approach progressively focuses on evidence m=
issing from the previous retrieval round. Vincent asked about the specific =
algorithm used by the judge controller; Daijiang noted that he would verify=
 the implementation details from the paper.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"fb320b4abc36" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/27-Q2reporting-=
ConfluenceSecurityandWebLayerProgress">Confluence Security and Web Layer Pr=
ogress</h3>
<p local-id=3D"eada964b223a">Guangyuan Mu reported that the Confluence work=
space has been created and that some members have uploaded technical docume=
nts. However, most members still need to upload their completed work.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a7588f5920fb">Suijie Song introduced the Web Layer=E2=80=99s=
 task allocation, including API documentation and CPI-function planning. Co=
mpleted features include string tabs, message persistence, and authenticati=
on. Tao asked about the CPI plan and current progress; Suijie confirmed tha=
t the related documentation is available in the shared folder.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"7cbc609eaf25" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/27-Q2reporting-=
DataProcessingLayerDevelopment">Data Processing Layer Development</h3>
<p local-id=3D"8cf9bcc99359">Guangyuan Mu presented the Data Processing Lay=
er=E2=80=99s completed semantic segmentation and card-system functionality.=
 A pre-compressor was added to calculate text weights, remove low-value con=
tent such as filler words, and use sentence similarity to create more natur=
al semantic segments.</p>
<p local-id=3D"54435dfcb3b0">After segmentation, the system groups sentence=
s by topic using a hash-table structure. When content exceeds a defined thr=
eshold, the system produces a summary and invokes an LLM to generate cards =
containing key content and keywords.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a74fd4732e68">Guangyuan also discussed link-type relationshi=
ps, including conflict, evidence, and support relationships, as well as tim=
estamp-based update mechanisms. Zeng Zhong=E2=80=99s Confluence document-pa=
rsing work was also mentioned.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"55437e03ba51" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/27-Q2reporting-=
RankingandBM25Improvements">Ranking and BM25 Improvements</h3>
<p local-id=3D"22b08a99aa47">Jiaxing Dai reported progress on adding a rank=
ing function and changing the BM25 tokenizer from Chinese to English. He te=
sted the system using an English financial information-retrieval dataset co=
ntaining 648 queries and 400 documents. The overall results were not yet sa=
tisfactory.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e5cef29f00ee">Vincent suggested exploring more flexible rank=
ing approaches for document chunks. The team discussed retrieval-quality an=
d embedding-segmentation issues. Vincent recommended testing higher-dimensi=
onal embedding models, approximately 1,000=E2=80=932,000 dimensions, and co=
nsidering an A2 model. He also noted that reducing chunk dimensions below 8=
0% could significantly weaken relevance.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"82cd88a34047" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/07/27-Q2reporting-=
CPRSystemEnhancement">CPR System Enhancement</h3>
<p local-id=3D"05678b59201f">Daijiang introduced CPR-system enhancements, i=
ncluding multi-turn execution and short-term memory, enabling the model to =
ask follow-up questions and retain conversational context.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4beed277de44">Huifang Liu presented the main user-request-pr=
ocessing components: intent classification, coreference resolution, and que=
ry rewriting. Seven question categories have been completed.</p>
<p local-id=3D"510ed965f560">The Monitoring Layer also demonstrated fronten=
d observability features, including real-time requests-per-second and P95-l=
atency monitoring, as well as automated API-metric collection. The team dis=
cussed confidentiality concerns around the document management system and a=
greed that the document-listing feature can be safely supported through acc=
ess-control mechanisms.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4bd8db74076e">The team will complete remaining layer-level i=
mprovements and prepare for integration testing next week.</p>
<p local-id=3D"07c208e10f73">=E6=98=9F=E6=9C=9F=E4=B8=8021:52</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
